cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use trae, please cite it as below."
title: "ZeroCode: Chinese-language AI coding skills for the Trae IDE"
abstract: >-
  ZeroCode is a rule pack for the Trae IDE aimed at people who write no code
  and read no English. The user states a goal in Chinese; the agent asks a
  couple of questions, picks a stack, writes the code, tests it, deploys it
  and returns the address. Installation is a single instruction pasted into
  the Trae chat box, with no configuration files to edit by hand.
